{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And YHWH will be for me Elohim</b> — this is not a condition, according to the words of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 28:21), but rather it is a vow, and its meaning is: if I return to my father's house, I will worship the special Name in the chosen land, at the site of this stone which shall be for me a house of Elohim, and there I will set aside the tithe. And there is in this matter a sod, from what they said (Ketubot 110a): whoever dwells outside the Land is like one who has no Elohim."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:20.892599492Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}